#
# A pinch does not scroll the page: gestures are one finger's.
#
# WPE's touch gesture controller (scrolling, taps) followed each touch
# event's first listed point, whatever the event was about, and took every
# finger's events as one finger's. A pinch scrolled the page by the jumps
# between the fingers, and a finger lifting ended that scroll with a fling;
# a second finger's touch-down even reached the controller as the first
# finger moving. Now the controller follows the point each event is about
# (NativeWebTouchEvent's fallback point is the event's own id), a second
# finger ends any scroll in progress without a fling (Phase::Cancelled
# starts no kinetic animation), and nothing is gestured until every finger
# is up. The page still gets every touch, and the embedder pinches. The
# controller keeps count of the fingers through touches the page handled.
# Measured on the Jolla Phone: a pinch that started as a one-finger drag
# kept scrolling the page 14 px back after the second finger; now it stops
# with the second finger.
#
